    "created_at": "2015-12-11T21:52:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-12-11T21:52:03Z",
    "body": "This is obviously super granular and interfaces could easily be coalesced into a larger `CanvasWriteMethods` interface. @junov-google do you have strong opinions here?\n\n`PaintRenderingContext2D` for Houdini CSS Paint API would look like:\n\n```\n[\n Constructor(unsigned long width, unsigned long height),\n Exposed=(Worklet)\n]\nPaintRenderingContext2D {\n};\nPaintRenderingContext2D implements CanvasStateMethods;\nPaintRenderingContext2D implements CanvasTransformationMethods;\nPaintRenderingContext2D implements CanvasCompositing;\nPaintRenderingContext2D implements CanvasImageSmoothing;\nPaintRenderingContext2D implements CanvasFillStrokeStyles;\nPaintRenderingContext2D implements CanvasShadowStyles;\nPaintRenderingContext2D implements CanvasDrawRectMethods;\nPaintRenderingContext2D implements CanvasDrawPathMethods;\nPaintRenderingContext2D implements CanvasTextMethods;\nPaintRenderingContext2D implements CanvasDrawImageMethods;\nPaintRenderingContext2D implements CanvasDrawingStyles;\nPaintRenderingContext2D implements CanvasPathMethods;\n```\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
