    "updated_at": "2015-12-12T00:59:33Z",
    "body": "I'm happy with super-granular if the people using it (i.e. Houdini and OffscreenCanvas) are happy.\n\nI'll compile and verify the output Monday to make sure nothing became wonky. One thing that we'll have to do (either you or the person who merges) is to squash into a single commit with no [bracketed prefix] at the beginning or period at the end, and a bit longer of a message description explaining why this change is being made. But we can wait until this is LGTMed.\n\nDoes this change any of the method ordering, as discussed in https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-whatwg-archive/2015Dec/0001.html ?\n\nI figure to merge this we'll want a LGTM from @junov for content, and I'll take editorial review responsibilities. If any of the other editors want to review, chime in so that I don't merge without your LGTM.\n",
