    "body": "On Mon, Dec 14, 2015 at 1:46 PM, Ian Kilpatrick notifications@github.com\nwrote:\n\n> @junov https://github.com/junov Splitting CanvasDrawingStyles isn't a\n> clear cut as addPathByStrokingText() and addText() methods take this\n> object assuming both Path and Text styles. I could add a another interface\n> which implements both PathDrawingStyles and TextDrawingStyles but seems\n> like overkill?\n> \n> The second option (another interface which implements both PathDrawingStyles\n>  and TextDrawingStyles) is what I meant to suggest.  The idea being that\n> should we go down the road not supporting text in v1 of OffscreenCanvas, we\n> could have OffscreenCanvasDrawingStyles that implements PathDrawingStyles,\n> but not TextDrawingStyles.\n> \n> @junov https://github.com/junov CanvasImageSmoothing is also used in\n> the spec for fill/stroke styles for patterns.\n> \n> Right.\n> \n> https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#fill-and-stroke-styles:dom-context-2d-imagesmoothingenabled\n> Belongs in separate because of that?\n> \n> What is the criterion for putting state attributes and methods into\n> separate sub-interfaces vs. leaving them in a general CanvasState\n> sub-interface\n> \n> @annevk https://github.com/annevk Added note about enumeration order\n> below IDL def.\n> \n> @domenic https://github.com/domenic Merged & renamed commit.\n> \n> —\n> Reply to this email directly or view it on GitHub\n> https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/396#issuecomment-164522975.\n",
